rem Sum of Squares
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=273
rem Add up the a, with 0 < a <= b, over
rem all N = a^2 + b^2 that are a product
rem of distinct primes = 1 mod 4 below
rem Limit

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Limit integer = 150

rem A prime p = u^2 + v^2 = (u + v i)
rem (u - v i). A product of some of
rem them, each in one of its two forms,
rem is a Gaussian integer z with
rem |z|^2 = N, and its 2^k forms give
rem the 2^(k-1) ways, each twice. So the
rem answer is half the sum of the
rem smaller of |re z| and |im z| over
rem all such z. List the z for two
rem halves of the primes, then multiply
rem every pair of them.
Ps = primes till Limit array
Quad' = Ps mod 4 equal 1
Ones = Ps filter Quad array
H = Ones len // 2
Ar = array 1
Ai = array 0
Br = array 1
Bi = array 0
for P in Ones
  Us = 1 to (P isqrt) array
  Vq = P - Us * Us
  Root = Vq isqrt
  Hit' = Root * Root equal Vq
  U = (Us filter Hit) 0
  V = (P - U * U) isqrt
  First = Ones take H
  Same' = First equal P
  Mine = (First filter Same) len
  if Mine greater 0
    Tr' = Ar * U - Ai * V
    Ti' = Ar * V + Ai * U
    Sr' = Ar * U + Ai * V
    Si' = Ai * U - Ar * V
    Ar = concat Ar Tr Sr
    Ai = concat Ai Ti Si
  else
    Tr' = Br * U - Bi * V
    Ti' = Br * V + Bi * U
    Sr' = Br * U + Bi * V
    Si' = Bi * U - Br * V
    Br = concat Br Tr Sr
    Bi = concat Bi Ti Si
  end
end
Total = 0
for I in 0 till (Ar len)
  Xr = Ar I
  Xi = Ai I
  Re' = Xr * Br - Xi * Bi
  Im' = Xr * Bi + Xi * Br
  Lo' = Re abs
  Hi' = Im abs
  Total += (Lo min Hi) sum
end
Answer = Total // 2
Answer print
